#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# matrix_exp

#% text
# `matrix_exp(m)` gives the matrix exponential of a square matrix.

#% text
# `matrix_exp(m, v)` gives `matrix_exp(m)` applied to the vector `v`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The same methods as `matrix_function(exp, m)`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
matrix_exp([[0, 1], [-1, 0]])
#% output
#= [[cos(1), sin(1)], [-sin(1), cos(1)]]

#% cell
matrix_exp([[1, 1], [0, 1]])
#% output
#= [[e, e], [0, e]]

#% subsection
# Scope

#% cell
matrix_exp([[1.0, 2.0], [3.0, 4.0]])
#% output
#= [[51.968956198705, 74.73656456700323], [112.10484685050479, 164.07380304920983]]

#% cell
matrix_exp([[0, 1], [0, 0]], [1, 1])
#% output
#= [2, 1]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `matrix_function`, `matrix_log`, `exp`
